# Human-reviewed GST facts backed by official Government of India sources.
{"id":"gst_definition","topic":"definition","question":"What is GST?","answer":"GST is a destination-based indirect tax levied on the supply of goods and services.","source_title":"CBIC - Know About GST","source_url":"https://cbic-gst.gov.in/about-gst.html","effective_from":"2017-07-01","verified_on":"2026-08-10"}
{"id":"gst_rate_structure","topic":"rates","question":"What are the main GST rate slabs in India now?","answer":"From 22 September 2025, the rationalised GST structure has a 5% merit rate and an 18% standard rate, with a special 40% de-merit rate for select goods and services.","source_title":"GST Council - Recommendations of the 56th Meeting","source_url":"https://www.gstcouncil.gov.in/sites/default/files/2025-09/press_release_press_information_bureau_0.pdf","effective_from":"2025-09-22","verified_on":"2026-08-10"}
{"id":"cgst_sgst","topic":"tax_components","question":"What is the difference between CGST and SGST?","answer":"For an intra-State supply, CGST is collected by the Central Government and SGST is collected by the State Government.","source_title":"CBIC - Know About GST","source_url":"https://cbic-gst.gov.in/about-gst.html","effective_from":"2017-07-01","verified_on":"2026-08-10"}
{"id":"igst_usage","topic":"tax_components","question":"When is IGST charged?","answer":"IGST is levied and collected by the Central Government on inter-State supplies of goods or services.","source_title":"CBIC - GST FAQ, Overview of the IGST Act","source_url":"https://cbic-gst.gov.in/pdf/new-faq-on-gst-second-edition.pdf","effective_from":"2017-07-01","verified_on":"2026-08-10"}
{"id":"healthcare_exemption","topic":"exemptions","question":"Are healthcare services exempt from GST?","answer":"Healthcare services provided by a clinical establishment, an authorised medical practitioner or paramedics are generally exempt from GST, subject to specified exceptions.","source_title":"CBIC Circular No. 32/06/2018-GST","source_url":"https://cbic-gst.gov.in/pdf/circularno-32-cgst.pdf","effective_from":"2017-07-01","verified_on":"2026-08-10"}
{"id":"education_exemption","topic":"exemptions","question":"Are educational services exempt from GST?","answer":"Specified services supplied by an eligible educational institution to its students, faculty and staff, and certain specified services supplied to eligible institutions, are exempt from GST; the exemption is not universal for every education-related service.","source_title":"CBIC Circular No. 177/09/2022-TRU and Notification No. 12/2017","source_url":"https://cbic-gst.gov.in/pdf/cir-177-08-2022-cgst.pdf","effective_from":"2017-07-01","verified_on":"2026-08-10"}
{"id":"mobile_phone_rate","topic":"goods_rates","question":"What is the GST rate on mobile phones?","answer":"Mobile phones classified under heading 8517 generally attract 18% GST.","source_title":"CBIC - GST Goods and Services Rates","source_url":"https://cbic-gst.gov.in/hindi/gst-goods-services-rates.html","verified_on":"2026-08-10"}
{"id":"restaurant_rate","topic":"services_rates","question":"What GST applies to restaurant services?","answer":"Restaurant service other than at specified premises generally attracts 5% GST without input tax credit, while restaurant service at specified premises generally attracts 18% GST with input tax credit.","source_title":"CBIC - GST Goods and Services Rates","source_url":"https://cbic-gst.gov.in/hindi/gst-goods-services-rates.html","verified_on":"2026-08-10"}
